# Authored on Windows, built on Unix CI runners (macOS and Ubuntu). Force LF on
# everything a runner executes: a CRLF run-block turns bash heredoc terminators
# (EOF, PY) into ones carrying a trailing carriage return, which never match
# their opener, and command substitutions inherit it too. It fails in ways that
# look nothing like a line-ending problem. core.autocrlf usually normalises the
# committed blob, but only this makes it deterministic regardless of each
# contributor's git config.
* text=auto

*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
